<title>HONG KONG: RUGBY UNION-FINAL DAY'S RESULTS IN WORLD CUP SEVENS.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-FINAL DAY'S RESULTS IN WORLD CUP SEVENS.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter-final results in the World Cup Sevens rugby union tournament on Sunday.</p>
<p>Fiji 56  South Korea 0</p>
<p>Western Samoa 21  England 5</p>
<p>South Africa 19  France 14</p>
<p>New Zealand 38  Australia 12</p>
<p>Semifinals</p>
<p>Fiji 38 Western Samoa 14</p>
<p>South Africa 31 New Zealand 7</p>
<p>Final Fiji 24 South Africa 21 (7-14)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Fiji - Tries: Marika Vunibaka 8th min, Luke Erenavula 12, Lemeki Koroi 14, 15. Conversions: Waisale Serevi 8, 12</p>
<p>South Africa - Tries: Andre Venter 2, 4, Stephen Brink 19. Conversions: Joost van der Westhuizen 2, 4, Brink 19</p>
</text>
